// Viktor learns Smart-ID at Eneli's library course, gets a phishing call and reports it (bank adviser Allan); a faked
// screenshot about the new girl Lenna spreads in the 4.b class chat while Helgi forwards a fake Smart-ID „news” to the
// family group (her neighbour Ilmar already „renewed”). One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner speaks
// at the 4.b parents' evening on children's online safety, takes part in the debate (ban or training) and writes a
// summary of the agreed rules for all families (059 Kasuta, Harno B2 summary with a comment, ~180 words).
// Grammar (B2, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5): nominalisation with -mine / -ja — andmete kogumine, otsuse tegemine,
// asukoha jälgimine, kasutaja, vastutaja; a verb sentence → a noun phrase and back, typical of written and official
// style — taught in 057 (the lecture's noun phrases noticed, rule table, style sorted; transformation both ways, the
// data-rules cloze; used in the Kasuta cards and the official mail to Liis), back in 058 (notice: PIN-koodide
// avaldamine = PIN-koode ei avaldata; the forms text) and 059 (the rules summary, rubric). 058 trains the impersonal
// (its title), 059 the quotative and hedging (väidetavalt, kooli sõnul, olevat) as a spiral of module 10.
// Harno B2 formats: radio interview (056 Harjuta), lecture gap fill (057 Avasta), problem article (057, 059 Harjuta),
